      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1119124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T03:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "or ... name the existing enum containing IPC_PROTOCOL_* and use\nthat as a type here.  not sure we have strict type checking on\nenums enabled, but hopefully coverity will catch any misuse.\n\nsame with the IPC_PEER_* enum.",
      "parentUuid": "1dd4bc8e_f3d70886",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "b3a57e3a27af3e576d0e0704c87cade6705f5286",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c2a5f99_b0a35fc9",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T05:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think validity of variable of enum type is checked in both compile time and run-time.\n\nEven although I don\u0027t think it is there but let\u0027s say there\u0027s compile time range check is there.\nI don\u0027t see big benefit using enum with name for protocol. Because I still need \"_COUNT\" in enum which is invalid as an input from user but should be used to check validity of protocol value from IPC. Due to this, even if I use enum XXX type, I still have to check if the protocol from user is _COUNT or not since _COUNT in enum but is not valid input from user.",
      "parentUuid": "5afcc749_9fe1ea6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "b3a57e3a27af3e576d0e0704c87cade6705f5286",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4a7026e_a09af087",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1119124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-19T02:08:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i\u0027m happy with doing a runtime bounds check.\n\nin addition to that, it\u0027s helpful to developers to specify\nthe type as an enum because that is a clear indication of\nwhat the valid inputs are.\n\ng++ would be stricter here than gcc, but we do run\ncoverity on the EC codebase, and i\u0027m hoping it\u0027ll\ncatch the cases that gcc won\u0027t.",
      "parentUuid": "3c2a5f99_b0a35fc9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 41
      },
